Titre Chin-Hui Liu : Myxomycetes  Enteridiaceae Taiwan
com$ Chin-Hui Liu adapt GF 06/2013
1,0$ référence  : Myxomycetes of Taiwan (XVIII): The Family Enteridiaceae -Taiwania, 51(4): 273-278, 2006
1,5$  Bibliographie
1,0$ Introduction : Enteridiaceae, one of the families of Liceales, is established by Farr (1982) due to the genus Reticularia has been replaced by Enteridium (Farr,1976). Members in this family are a group of Myxomycetes with fructifications often large and conspicuous, and in the form of aethalium or pseudoaethalium except Tubifera bombarda which is a sporangiate form. Other distinct characters of this family are the presence of pseudocapillitiumin in various forms, and the absence of true capillitium.///The lacking of dictydine granules is a character separating this family from Cribrariaceae. Four genera are generally accepted in this family althouth one of them, Dictydiaethalium, was removed (Nannenga-Bremekamp, 1985).

1,2 $ Fructification sporangiate; sporangia clustered or united into a pseudoaethalium
1,3 $ Fructification aethaliate
2,cs3 $ Fructification sporangiate or pseudoaethaliate with persistent peridium; hypothallus massive, fibrous or spongy $ Tubifera$s"Tubifera"
2,0 $ Fructification pseudoaethaliate; peridia evanescent at maturity except for thickened strands at the angles, which persist as pseudocapillitial threads depending from the lids; hypothallus not massive or spongy $ Dictydiaethalium
3,cs2 $ Aethalium subglobose to conical or pulvinate, often on a restricted base; pseudocapillitium of colorless, ornamented tubes; spores in mass pinkish, then pallid $ Lycogala$s"Lycogala"
3,cs1 $ Aethalium pulvinate on a broad base; pseudocapillitium of frayed or perforated membranes; spores in mass brown, yellow or olivaceous $ Enteridium$s"Enteridium"
5,0$Chen, Y.-F., P.-A. Yea, J.-H. Chang and C.-H. Liu.  2005. Myxomycetes in Hsien-Chi-Yen, Taipei  City. Coll. and Res. 18: 15-23.///Farr, M. L. 1976. Reticularia Baumgarten (Lichens)  versus Reticularia Bulliard (Myxomycetes).  Taxon 25: 514.///Farr, M. L. 1982. Notes on Myxomycetes III.  Mycologia 74: 339-343.///Ing, B. 1999. The Myxomycete of Britain and  Ireland. The Richmond Publication Co. Ltd.,  England, UK. 374pp.///Liu, C.-H. 1980. Myxomycetes of Taiwan I.  Taiwania 25: 141-151.///Liu, C.-H. 1981. Myxomycetes of Taiwan II.  Taiwania 26: 58-67.///Liu, C.-H. 1982. Myxomycetes of Taiwan III.  Taiwania 27: 64-85.///Martin, G. W. and C. J. Alexopoulos. 1969. The  Myxomycetes. Univ. Iowa Press, Iowa City,USA. 477pp.

